    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will deploy a containerized application using Docker and Kubernetes, integrating with required APIs, including civil-status and town-planning software, EDM systems (such as Alfresco and Maarch Courrier), and user directories (like Active Directory and Keycloak). Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "LLM model, Mistral 7B Instruct, will provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, while Nexus Engineering S.r.l. explainability tools (SHAP and LIME) ensure transparency and accuracy. To meet the performance requirement of a response time lower than 2 seconds, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will optimize an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval using quantization methods like INT8 or auto-scaling." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expect a p95 response time of approximately 1800ms, which is close to the required limit. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. high availability architecture design using Terraform and Ansible for infrastructure provisioning and configuration management will ensure an objective of 99.9% availability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For GDPR compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. guarantee the EU data hosting, encryption of sensitive data using anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, and implementation of access control standards, including multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC). Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA) capability will assess the impact of Nexus Engineering S.r.l. AI-powered information systems on personal data protection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. subcontracting policy requires all subcontractors to be the EU-established, reducing cross-border data flow risks. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a source code escrow capability in place with Logitas, a French provider, to mitigate vendor lock-in risks. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval will also adhere to the principles of transparency, fairness, and accountability in AI decision-making processes as required by the EU AI Act." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The estimated annual revenue from this project is approximately 750,000 euros per year, based on a total contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target a gross margin percentage of 28% and will focus on optimizing variable costs (65% of project costs) to ensure the expected service quality while maintaining a competitive price." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To reduce energetic consumption, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose leveraging green hosting partners like OVHcloud or Scaleway, which utilize 100% renewable energy. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantization and auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, can reduce energetic consumption by approximately 35% compared to Nexus Engineering S.r.l. baseline. ### Unaddressed Requirements None of the requirements from the tender have been left unaddressed in a comprehensive tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval. ### Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is committed to delivering a high-quality AI solution that meets the City of Belval requirements for an intelligent assistance tool. a comprehensive tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval combines expertise in AI/ML systems, GDPR compliance, security, and sustainability to provide a comprehensive solution that enhances municipal agents' daily missions while respecting regulatory constraints and minimizing environmental impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval offers significant value and look forward to the opportunity to implement an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out. The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories. Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services. An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation. {     \"TechnicalArchitect Agent\": \"The client requires: response time < 2 seconds, 99.9% availability, API integration with civil-status and town-planning software, EDM and user directories. Hosting must be on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the European Union." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No dependency on non-European suppliers. The solution should provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. Can our current stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do you propose?\",     \"Budget Agent\": \"The total contract value is 3 million euros over 4 years. Annual exploitation costs must stay within the local authority's budget capacity. The client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Are we financially eligible to bid, and what is the projected margin? How can we optimize costs while ensuring the expected service quality?\",     \"SecurityCompliance Agent\": \"The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only hosting, no data transfer outside the European Union, encryption of sensitive data). All AI recommendations must be explainable post-hoc. No automated decision is allowed without explicit agent validation. What security measures do we need to implement to ensure the proposed solution compliance with GDPR and other regulatory requirements?\",     \"Legal Agent\": \"The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (the European Union-only hosting, no data transfer outside the European Union, encryption of sensitive data)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "All AI recommendations must be explainable post-hoc. No automated decision is allowed without explicit agent validation. What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the regulatory requirements? How can we ensure that our solution respects the rights of users and meets the expectations of the local authority?\",     \"AIInnovation Agent\": \"The client expects a solution that provides intelligent assistance to municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution should be able to contextualize answers based on agent demands, assist with drafting administrative contents, and provide relevant information for file analysis and processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message1> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy can we propose to meet these requirements?\",     \"CSRSustainability Agent\": \"City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. How can we ensure that our proposed solution meets these sustainability requirements and reduces the environmental impact?\" }" ;
