    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can we ensure that we solution respects the rights of users and meets the expectations of the local authority? Based on the provided context, we have experience with GDPR compliance and have standard legal instruments in place, including a Data Processing Agreement template version 3.2. we default legal basis for processing personal data is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest. we also have DPIA support available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the tender requirements, the main legal risks to flag are related to GDPR compliance and AI explainability. However, we has a no automated decision without human validation policy, which aligns with the requirement for explicit agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we are aware of the EU AI Act and the EU AI Act implications on transparency obligations and human oversight. To ensure compliance with regulatory requirements and respect for user rights, we should emphasize we commitment to intra-EU operations only, which eliminates the need for Standard Contractual Clauses or adequacy decisions. we should also highlight we ability to provide explainable AI recommendations post-hoc and we adherence to the principle of human validation for automated decisions. we subcontracting policy requires all subcontractors to be EU-established, which further reduces cross-border data flow risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
